    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d160">

                <pb facs="0139" n="131" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg131"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.92/27: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Thailand</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-19T20:00:00-04:00">September 19, 1940—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>50. Your 81, September 17, 4 p.m. On September 19 the Thai Minister called at his
                    request on an officer of the Department and presented an <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi><anchor n="88" xml:id="d160-f1"/> in reply to the oral
                    communication made to the Thai Minister here on September 11.<anchor n="89"
                        xml:id="d160-f2"/> The officer of the Department said, in response to the
                    Thai Minister’s request, that he would be glad to bring the Thai <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> to the attention of the Secretary of
                    State. The officer of the Department restated to the Thai Minister briefly the
                    views expressed in the Department’s 37, August 21, 6 p.m., and 46, September 11,
                    5 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d160-f1" n="88" xml:id="d160-f1-content">
